  "notes": "specs/03 A4's fixture, and the only genuinely ISSUED certificate in the corpus. Five pages: the ACORD 25 on page 1 and three endorsements behind it — RSCG 03 03 09 21 (blanket additional insured, pages 2-3), CG 24 04 12 19 (waiver of subrogation, page 4) and CG 20 01 12 19 (primary and non-contributory, page 5). ADDL INSD and SUBR WVD are printed as the letter Y, not as ticks. The description of operations names RSCG0303, CG2001 and CG2404, all three hedged with 'where required by written contract', so all three are conditional. The same three forms appear again as attached endorsement pages, which is a different context and therefore a separate mention. PERSONAL DATA (kb-samples MANIFEST rule 4, which left C2 UNVERIFIED for the labeller to settle): the CONTACT NAME, PHONE, FAX and E-MAIL boxes are all empty, and the producer is a company with a licence number. The AUTHORIZED REPRESENTATIVE box carries an ink signature that reads as a person's name; it is an image, it is not extracted as a value, and the name is listed in redacted-names.json so that no output, prompt, help article or marketing string can carry it. The fixture is kept. The automobile block is empty apart from a stray '4077887933' printed in its type column; the number is not a policy number, a date or a limit, and it is not labelled as one.",
